pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* Positive companion to
* incorrect/version2/order_definition_strengthening_to_core: the mode switch
* where it belongs, on the same formula.
*
* At the top level `strengthening_to_core on` moves the real database to core,
* and that move is exactly what makes `add_derived_goals = false` sound for
* every `red` after it -- there is no longer a derived set for the mode to
* drop. Inside the order definition it moved the empty order sub-database
* while setting the same global flag, leaving the outer derived set unmoved
* and the promise unkept. Ordered this way the `red` is legitimate and the
* proof verifies; ordered the other way round, with `1 y1 >= 1` already in the
* derived set, the mode switch cannot rescue it -- see
* incorrect/version2/strengthening_to_core_bare_red_derived.
f 1
strengthening_to_core on
red 1 y1 >= 1 ; y1 -> 1 ;
output NONE
conclusion NONE
end pseudo-Boolean proof
